 it all sticks  together  form your patties with your hands and  then put them back in your skillet  make sure they get really crispy on both  sides toast a brioche bun  and then add some spicy mayo top with  avocado and don't forget your lime and  salt  hi drew i'm seyran from legally  plant-based and i'm so excited to show  you how to make a delicious snack  using a norishi start by cutting the  nori sheet and then add your tofu katsu  add some sushi rice top it with some  roasted sesame seeds  add carrots cabbage and some sliced  avocado  add spicy mayo a slice of vegan cheddar  some more rice some ketchu sauce and  crispy onions  then just fold it clockwise  and there you have it hey drew it's  marlon shotland with urban bliss life  and today i'm going to show you how to  make these super easy  super tasty airfryer chicken wings  first lightly oil the inside of your air  fryer basket or airfryer trays with  vegetable oil or olive oil spray  next place the chicken wings in a bowl  and pat them dry  sprinkle arrowroot starch over the wings  to coat them evenly  you can also use cornstarch instead  season the wings with salt and pepper  then place them in a single layer in  your airfryer basket or airfryer trays  airfry at 380 degrees fahrenheit for 12  minutes  then flip over the wings increase the  heat to 400 degrees fahrenheit  and airfry them for another 12 minutes  these chicken wings  are perfectly crispy on the outside and  tender and juicy on the inside  so easy right hey drew it's the perfect  time of year to make julia child's booth  bourguignon let me show you how i make  it  first dry three pounds of beef chuck  well with paper towels and season  generously with salt and pepper  working in batches sear the meat on all  sides cut  thick slices of bacon into half inch  pieces  add two thinly sliced onions and cook  until browned and caramelized peel two  large carrots and parsnips and cut into  large pieces  add the vegetables season with salt and  pepper then add two tablespoons flour  and three tablespoons tomato paste  stir to coat and cook for about two  minutes add three cups of beef stock and  wine reserving a glass for dinner bring  to a simmer and add the brown meat a  bundle of thyme one pound of brown  mushrooms and some pearl onions  cook in a 325 degree oven for about two  hours  serve over some creamy mashed potatoes  and top with fresh parsley  cheers drew happy cooking hi drew thanks  for having me back  on the show today i'm going to show you  how to tackle steak  it's always better to season your steak  with salt ahead of time a few hours is  fine but overnight is ideal this will  allow the salt to penetrate all the way  through to the center of the steak set  this on a wire rack and place it in your  fridge  uncovered for airflow if you got an  instant pot they all come with this  little rack how do you know when your  pan is hot and with this hack you will  forever get a good sear on your steak  every single time drop a teaspoon of  water into your pan and when it looks  like team 1000 out of terminator it  means your pan is ready  this is called the leidenfrost effect  and if your water sticks and bubbles out  means your pan is too cold and it's not  ready  for new york strips i like to add zero  oil fat side down first  render out that fat and then sear both  sides for about two minutes per side  when you're ready to butter base turn  down the heat to low because butter  burns at high temperatures which can  leave  burnt bitter taste onto the steak and  butter absolutely loves aromatics like  thyme and garlic because they're good  buddies and they infuse  really really well together a digital  thermometer is a must  always remove the steak 10 degrees lower  than your desired doneness because the  steak will continue to cook even when  it's out of the pan cover and let it  rest  resting allows the muscle proteins to  relax so it can retain more of its own  juices  and flavor i like to make a quick sauce  using horseradish a mustard  salt and pepper i always cut my steaks  at a bias because it always makes for a  better  meat fan and finally don't sleep on the  resting juices  this is where the magic is at now watch  this move whoa  now you tell me if this will taste good  or not  and that's how you cook a steak wow i'm  in a delicious  food coma just for watching that  [Music]  you

